### 2. Participating in the IETF
* **Presentation**: Sean Turner presented [New Participant Program - Session 2 - Participating in the IETF](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-newparticipant-sessa-new-participant-program-session-2-participating-in-the-ietf-00).
* **Communication Channels**:
  * Email mailing lists are the primary venue for IETF work (~500 active lists). Meetings discuss issues, but consensus must be confirmed on the working group mailing lists.
  * Main list categories: `ietf-announce`, `id-announce`, `irtf-announce`, working group lists, BoF lists, `ietf` (general discussion), and `ietf-last-call`.
  * **Mail Etiquette**: Plain text/ASCII formatting, succinct replies, clear subject lines, inline/bottom-reply style.
* **Data Tracker & Technical Tools**:
  * **Data Tracker** (`datatracker.ietf.org`): Central document management system for draft status, IPR disclosures, working group charters, schedules, diffs, and meeting materials.
  * **Meetecho**: Online participation tool integrating video, live transcription, Zulip chat, remote mic queues, and show-of-hands polling.
  * **Zulip**: Chat system paired with Meetecho sessions.
  * **On-Site Logistics**: Scanning session QR codes enters attendees into the Meetecho queue and assists with room sizing.
* **Badges & Lanyards**:
  * Red lanyards indicate request for no photography.
  * Colored dots indicate leadership/roles (e.g., Blue dot for Working Group Chairs; specific dots for IESG, IAB, LLC, IRSG, NomCom).
* **New Participant Support Programs**:
  * **Guides Program**: Matches first-time attendees one-on-one with experienced mentors based on technical interests (highlighted by Michelle Cotton).
  * **Quick Connections**: Speed-networking session connecting new participants with leadership and experienced community members.
* **Q&A & Chat Discussion**:
  * *Antonio Carismo* asked how first-time participants can find mentors to navigate the large community without feeling intimidated. Sean Turner and Michelle Cotton detailed the Guides Program and Quick Connections event.
  * Chat discussion: *Eisha Raazia* asked for advice for undergrads and how to network remotely. *Steve Traugott* responded that undergrads and recent grads drive significant innovation in technical communities. Michelle Cotton advised using Meetecho direct messaging during sessions.
  * Chat discussion: *Edgar Orendain* noted a minor correction for presentation slide text regarding redundant phrasing ("OIDC" instead of "OIDC Connect").
  * Chat discussion: *Steve Traugott* shared a UI troubleshooting tip that setting Chrome browser zoom to 150% revealed the Meetecho top navigation icons (collaboration tools, queue, transcripts).

